From 80c8cbe7872dfbb62be963520a484931c3e94046 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MarsInsanity <mazemoyux@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 05:20:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add the Anbernic RG351P (dArkMoss rg351p unit)

The RG351P runs dArkMoss's rg351p unit: the rg351 kernel with
rk3326-rg351p-linux.dtb, one SD slot with spruce on the SPRUCEOS partition,
SPRUCE_PLATFORM="RG351P". It shares the V10's panel (320x480 portrait shown
as 480x320), SoC, PMIC and codec, so display, CPU, DRAM and audio follow
V10.cfg. What differs:

- Pad: an internal USB HID controller, "OpenSimHardware OSH PB Controller"
  (1209:3100), with the d-pad on a hat (ABS_HAT0X/Y). It has no by-path
  link, so it is found by name. Button codes (A 304, B 305, X 306, Y 307,
  L1 308, R1 309, Start 310, Select 311, L3 312, R3 313, L2 314, R2 315) are
  ArkOS's RG351P es_input.cfg. RetroArch 1.22's udev joypad driver numbers
  KEY_UP..KEY_DOWN and the pad's nine mouse buttons first, so in RetroArch
  they are 15-26 (A 15 ... R2 26); SDL numbers 304 first, so DraStic keeps
  0-11. Checked on hardware: with 0-11 only the hat d-pad and stick worked.
- No menu button: SELECT+START (the V10's chord) or the stick click is MENU.
  As on the RGB30, B_L3 is DOESNT_EXIST: the pad is a HID keyboard the
  kernel autorepeats, and a held click's repeats matched menubutton_watchdog's
  "key $B_L3" cancel and cancelled the press (seen on hardware).
  PyUI ignores the stick axes in the menus (their range is not the V10's
  +-1800 the darkmoss provider is sized for).
- Volume is a hardware wheel after the codec: the codec stays at full and
  stored volume at max (a temporary sleep mute aside), and PyUI hides the
  volume setting and indicator (supports_volume, as the Miyoo Mini).
- Rumble is on pwm0, not a force-feedback pad: vibrate drives the PWM through
  sysfs and always leaves it disabled.

New: platform RG351P.cfg/.sh, PyUI rg351p.py and rg351p-system.json,
RetroArch defaults and an autoconfig for the pad, DraStic config translated
from the V10's, first-boot flag. RG351P added next to V10 in
helperFunctions.sh (ANBERNIC_RG351P), PyUI launch.sh and device_factory.py,
drastic_functions.sh and the app launchers.

PyUI key mapping checked against this tree's PyUI. Not yet run on hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
